    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0534" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Rumania)/7–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 306<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Representative in Rumania
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Melbourne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d306-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-08T20:00:00+02:00">July 8, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>457. Yesterday the King expressed to me his bewilderment in being awarded the
                    Soviet Order of Victory by Marshal Stalin and in being given two
                    airplanes by the Russians since his past experience has been that the Russians
                    have most realistic motives for their actions (my 451, July 4<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d306-f2"/>). (Rptd Moscow as 122)
                    He plainly distrusts these sudden gestures of amiability.</p>
                <pb facs="0535" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/>
                <p>Rumors have spread that the permission to grant Rumania 16 army divisions (my 449, July 3<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d306-f3"/>) was accompanied by the signature of a Rumanian-Soviet
                    military pact but the King stated that he had been told that this was not the
                    case.</p>
                <p>At present in common with the bulk of Rumanians the King expressed hopes that the
                    impending Potsdam conference would give a reasonable interpretation to the Yalta
                    declaration and secure a truly representative govt for Rumania.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Melbourne</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
